Proof this bug was REAL and nondeterministic (2026-09-01), captured while
building src/__tests__/integration/report-entry-classes-order.test.ts
against the UNFIXED code (before src/lib/class-labels.ts's
sortEntryClassesByShowClassOrder existed and before the three query sites
called it). Command run twice, back to back, no code or data changes
between runs:

  DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/remi_test npx vitest run \
    src/__tests__/integration/report-entry-classes-order.test.ts

=== RUN 1 — 3 of 3 failed ================================================

 ❯ src/__tests__/integration/report-entry-classes-order.test.ts (3 tests | 3 failed) 314ms
   × Reports — a multi-class dog prints its classes in show running order, not DB return order > Exhibitor List (catalogue-order-xlsx) lists classes in running order regardless of insertion order 165ms
     → expected '10, 1' to be '1, 10' // Object.is equality
   × Reports — a multi-class dog prints its classes in show running order, not DB return order > Absentee report (absentee-report-xlsx) lists classes in running order regardless of insertion order 73ms
     → expected '10. Open; 1. Minor Puppy' to be '1. Minor Puppy; 10. Open' // Object.is equality
   × Reports — a multi-class dog prints its classes in show running order, not DB return order > Financial Statement (financial-statement-xlsx) lists classes in running order regardless of insertion order 73ms
     → expected 'Open; Minor Puppy' to be 'Minor Puppy; Open' // Object.is equality

 Test Files  1 failed (1)
      Tests  3 failed (3)

=== RUN 2 (immediately after, same data/code) — 2 of 3 failed ============

   × Reports — a multi-class dog prints its classes in show running order, not DB return order > Exhibitor List (catalogue-order-xlsx) lists classes in running order regardless of insertion order 163ms
   × Reports — a multi-class dog prints its classes in show running order, not DB return order > Absentee report (absentee-report-xlsx) lists classes in running order regardless of insertion order 78ms
   ✓ Reports — a multi-class dog prints its classes in show running order, not DB return order > Financial Statement (financial-statement-xlsx) lists classes in running order regardless of insertion order 67ms

 Test Files  1 failed (1)
      Tests  2 failed | 1 passed (3)

=== Why two different results matter =====================================

The SAME test, against the SAME unfixed code and the SAME kind of fixture
data (each test builds its own show), produced a DIFFERENT pass/fail
pattern across two consecutive runs. That is the whole bug in one
observation: Drizzle's relational query for entries.entryClasses carries
no ORDER BY on a joined table's column, so Postgres's return order for that
relation is genuinely undefined — sometimes it happens to match show
running order (a false green), sometimes it doesn't (a red that would look
like a real regression to anyone bisecting it).

